# Testing ritual

Read [docs/TESTING-PLAYBOOK.md](docs/TESTING-PLAYBOOK.md) for full golden paths.

## When to proactively suggest testing

| Situation | Suggest |
|-----------|---------|
| Finished implementing backlog story(ies) in `src/` or `tests/` | Layer 1 docker test + Layer 2 Agent B for touched story IDs + focused smoke |
| User asks to mark story Done or flip `@done` | Agent B spec compliance first; do not update tags without coverage |
| User reports app "feels wrong" | FINDING template → map to Gherkin → classify before fixing |
| User closes a phase or epic | Full golden path + Agent B on all Must stories + SMOKE-LOG entry |
| User only changed docs | Skip docker test unless they ask |

## What to say (short)

After non-trivial implementation, end with:

1. **Regression:** `docker compose --profile test run --rm test`
2. **Spec:** Fresh chat → `Read .cursor/skills/spec-compliance-review/SKILL.md and review story {ID}`
3. **Smoke:** Link playbook section (Phase 4 golden path or story-specific steps)

## Agent roles

- **This chat (Agent A):** implement; add tests when assertable; do not self-certify `@done`
- **Fresh chat (Agent B):** read-only spec compliance; run docker tests; report GAPs

## Smoke finding format

When user describes unexpected behavior, ask them to fill or infer:

`Observed` / `Expected` / `Story ID` / `Route` / `Severity`

Then recommend Agent B before code changes.
